From a63fa7ab72e217c596511eb8876afc867fab26e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: horizon-prism <horizon-prism@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:06:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add fork branding (M6)

- HORIZON_FORK (OFF by default) renames the binary to horizon-prism, the
  bundle to dev.playhorizon.HorizonPrismLauncher and the internal name to
  HorizonPrismLauncher, which gives the fork its own data folder
  (~/Library/Application Support/HorizonPrismLauncher) and its own
  HORIZONPRISMLAUNCHER_DATA_DIR, so it can live beside Prism;
- program_info keeps Prism's artwork files as inputs but writes them under
  the fork's installed names; the Qt resource keeps the name
  prismlauncher.qrc because main.cpp calls Q_INIT_RESOURCE(prismlauncher);
- macOS install destinations follow the bundle CMake actually produces
  (horizon-prism.app, from OUTPUT_NAME), so the icon lands in the right
  bundle;
- the GitHub updater points at this repository on Windows and Linux;
  Sparkle is disabled on macOS because the fork has no key, and Prism's
  feed would offer upstream releases;
- .github/workflows/horizon.yml builds and tests the fork on macOS, Linux
  and Windows and uploads an unsigned macOS artifact.

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
